      "result": "Perfect! I have completed the testing of all 16 checklist items for the technical specifications knowledge base application.\n\n## Test Summary\n\n**Results: 15 PASSED, 1 FAILED**\n\n### Passing Tests (15/16):\n✅ **FT-1**: Module filtering works - selecting a module shows only its documents, \"All\" restores complete list\n✅ **FT-2**: Document view displays title, version, update date, content sections, and related documents\n✅ **FT-3**: Clicking related document links navigates to those documents\n✅ **FT-4**: Collapsing sections hides their content\n✅ **FT-5**: Expanding sections restores their content and links\n✅ **FT-6**: Graph nodes can be selected with visual feedback, zoom controls work (100%→120%→reset)\n✅ **FT-7**: Graph has 19 nodes (one per document) with 35 connections for relationships\n✅ **FT-8**: All three tabs (Documents, Knowledge Graph, Favorites) are accessible\n✅ **FT-9**: Application state preserved across tabs (selected document, section expand/collapse states, graph zoom)\n✅ **FT-10**: Favorites persisted after reload, count updated, markers survived filtering\n✅ **CS-12**: No documents reference themselves in related docs or section links\n✅ **CS-13**: Graph correctly represents all documents and their relationships\n✅ **IX-15**: Section toggle indicators visually show expanded/collapsed state\n✅ **IX-17**: Collapsed section links display \"Expand section to access link\" prompt; work after expansion\n✅ **IX-18**: No-results message appears for empty searches; clearing search restores documents\n\n### Failing Tests (1/16):\n❌ **IX-16**: Clicking graph nodes only selects them; document view doesn't open without manually switching to Documents tab\n\nThe application successfully implements most of the requested functionality with strong support for document browsing, section management, favorites, module filtering, and state preservation across tabs. The primary limitation is that the knowledge graph doesn't directly open documents when nodes are clicked.",
